      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument for prioritizing gender identity over biological sex in elite athletics is seen as problematic because critics argue it prioritizes lived experience over physiological data that directly determines physical performance capabilities. Since competitive fairness relies on ensuring athletes can compete under equal biological conditions, proponents of the strict \"ensign\" (safe and fair) line believe that transgender women may still hold an unfair advantage due to the irreversible impact of testosterone on muscle mass and bone density. While support for inclusivity is strong in many social and community sports, the integrity of high-stakes competition is often defended by the necessity of using objective, pre-hormone biological sex as the definitive baseline for elimination.",
